        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s1"
      },
      "text": "Cylance SPEAR™ has identified an APT group which deploys multiple customized malware implants, targeting mainly Chinese and Russian users.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_2",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Cylance_The_Ghost_Dragon(04-22-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s2"
      },
      "text": "Cylance determined that the ‘Ghost Dragon’ group utilized specifically tailored variants of Gh0st RAT , which the group modified from the 3.6 version of the source code released in 2008.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_3",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Cylance_The_Ghost_Dragon(04-22-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s3"
      },
      "text": "Newly implemented security mechanisms in the altered malware makes identification of Gh0st RAT Command and Control network traffic more difficult for both security products and researchers.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_4",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Cylance_The_Ghost_Dragon(04-22-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s4"
      },
      "text": "This write-up provides initial disclosure of a portion of the malware and infrastructure used by the Ghost Dragon group and covers the new security mechanisms in detail, as well as revealing how researchers were able to communicate with the custom implant by rebuilding and compiling a customized Gh0st RAT controller.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_5",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Cylance_The_Ghost_Dragon(04-22-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s1"
      },
      "text": "After the packet flag, packet length and unzip length have been verified, a working connection is created between the victim and the controller.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_7",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Cylance_The_Ghost_Dragon(04-22-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s3"
      },
      "text": "Changes to the Gh0st RAT Protocol In an older version of the customized Gh0st RAT malware, the protocol packet flag is no longer represented by the string ‘Gh0st’.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_8",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Cylance_The_Ghost_Dragon(04-22-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s4"
      },
      "text": "The Ghost Dragon group modified the source code and changed the packet flag to ‘XYTvn’, as seen in Figure 4.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
